stave 1

/// A mitre: two parts meeting at a corner, each cut on the diagonal so the
/// joint line runs from the outside corner to the inside corner and no end
/// grain shows. A picture frame's corners, a mitred box's corners, a
/// mitred face frame.
///
/// Draw the parts the way the frame looks before it is mitred: square to
/// each other and crossing at the corner, each running right to the
/// outside of it. Each part gives up the half of the crossing at its own
/// end. Parts of the same width meet at 45deg; parts of different widths
/// meet on the line from corner to corner, as a mitre between them is cut.
///
/// A mitre is glued end grain to end grain, so it is the weakest of the
/// glued corners: for a frame that takes a load, choose a half lap or a
/// mortise and tenon instead.
kind mitre : joint {
  roles {
    piece: Parts
    into:  Parts
  }

  cut piece_mitre: crossing(piece, into) {
    diagonal()
  }
  cut into_mitre: crossing(into, piece) {
    diagonal()
  }

  note: "Cut every mitre with the same saw setting and check one corner is square before cutting the rest; glue with a band clamp so all four corners close at once"
}
